### ====================================================================
### ApexDrive Bharat - MERN REST API Demonstration (VS Code)
### Covers Experiment 5 (REST API), Exp 6 (MongoDB CRUD), Exp 7 (JWT)
### ====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@jwtToken = 

### --------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Health Check & MongoDB Connectivity (Exp 5 & 6)
### --------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Content-Type: application/json

### ====================================================================
### EXPERIMENT 6: MONGODB VEHICLE FLEET CRUD OPERATIONS
### ====================================================================

### 1. READ: Get All Vehicles from MongoDB
GET {{baseUrl}}/cars
Content-Type: application/json

### 2. READ: Get Vehicles Filtered by Category (SUV)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cars?category=suv
Content-Type: application/json

### 3. READ: Get Single Vehicle by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/cars/1
Content-Type: application/json

### 4. CREATE: Add New Vehicle to MongoDB (CRUD Create)
POST {{baseUrl}}/cars
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "make": "Tata",
  "model": "Harrier Dark Edition",
  "type": "Executive Urban SUV",
  "category": "suv",
  "price": 3199,
  "passengers": 5,
  "transmission": "Automatic",
  "fuel": "Kryotec 2.0L Diesel",
  "image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1549399542-7e3f8b79c341?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=800"
}

### 5. UPDATE: Edit Vehicle Rental Rate in MongoDB (CRUD Update)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/cars/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 3799,
  "available": true
}

### 6. DELETE: Remove Vehicle from MongoDB (CRUD Delete)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/cars/6
Content-Type: application/json


### ====================================================================
### EXPERIMENT 6: MONGODB RESERVATION BOOKINGS CRUD OPERATIONS
### ====================================================================

### 1. READ: Get All Bookings
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

### 2. CREATE: New Reservation in MongoDB (CRUD Create)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "carId": 1,
  "carMake": "Mahindra",
  "carModel": "Thar 4x4",
  "carType": "Off-Road SUV",
  "pickupLocation": "Mumbai Central Hub",
  "returnLocation": "Goa Coastal Hub",
  "pickupDate": "2026-10-01",
  "returnDate": "2026-10-05",
  "days": 4,
  "customerName": "Samruddh Jadhav",
  "customerEmail": "samruddh.jadhav@ves.ac.in",
  "customerPhone": "+91 98201 45678",
  "licenseNumber": "MH02-2023-0091823",
  "totalAmount": 16515
}

### 3. UPDATE: Change Booking Status in MongoDB (CRUD Update)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/bookings/BK-IN-670793/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Ongoing"
}

### 4. READ: Dashboard Analytics from MongoDB Aggregation
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/stats
Content-Type: application/json


### ====================================================================
### EXPERIMENT 7: USER AUTHENTICATION & JWT SECURITY
### ====================================================================

### 1. User Registration (Password Hashed with Bcrypt + JWT Issued)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Samruddh Jadhav",
  "email": "samruddh.jadhav@ves.ac.in",
  "phone": "+91 98201 45678",
  "city": "Mumbai",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "admin"
}

### 2. User Login (Authenticates with Bcrypt & Returns JWT Token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "samruddh.jadhav@ves.ac.in",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 3. Protected Route (Requires Valid JWT Bearer Token)
# Copy the token received from login and paste it after Bearer:
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
